[2026-07-22T21:01:21.737Z] [INFO]           "prompt": "I'm analyzing CI/CD best practices for the repo link-assistant/formal-ai (issue #828). I need you to gather reference material from external repositories and report back concise, factual findings.\n\nPlease do the following using the `gh` CLI (it is authenticated) and/or WebFetch:\n\n1. Fetch the CI/CD best-practices doc: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md — summarize its key rules/principles as a bullet list (especially anything about: flaky tests, test isolation, deterministic tests, false positives/negatives, warnings-as-errors, retries, timeouts, concurrency, caching, matrix builds).\n\n2. List the GitHub Actions workflow files in each of these template repos (use `gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/contents/.github/workflows`):\n   - link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n   - link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n   - link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n   For the Rust template, fetch the main CI workflow file content and note: how it runs clippy (does it use -D warnings?), how it handles test determinism/flakiness, whether it uses concurrency groups, timeouts on jobs, and any retry logic.\n\n3. Report a concise structured summary. Do NOT clone repos. Keep it factual with the actual settings you observe. Include the raw list of workflow filenames per template repo.\n\nReturn your findings as plain text (they will be saved to a research file). Include direct quotes for the most important best-practice rules.",
