[2026-07-22T21:01:53.516Z] [INFO]         "content": "# CI/CD Best Practices - Key Rules & Principles\n\n## Document Section Headings\n\n1. Why CI/CD Matters for AI Development\n2. Recommended CI/CD Templates\n3. Key CI/CD Principles\n   - Run Checks Only on Relevant File Changes\n   - File Size Limits\n   - Automated Code Formatting\n   - Static Analysis & Linting\n   - Fast-Fail Job Ordering\n   - Changeset-Based Versioning\n   - Validate the Actual Merge Result\n   - Pre-commit Hooks\n   - Release Automation\n   - Concurrency Control\n   - Secrets Detection\n   - Documentation Validation\n4. Quality Enforcement Strategy\n5. Getting Started\n6. Automatic CI/CD Remediation\n\n## Key Rules & Principles\n\n**Fast-Fail Ordering:** The document emphasizes running \"fast checks (~7-30s each)\" before \"slow checks (~1-10 min each)\" to deliver rapid feedback on compile status, linting, and file limits before running comprehensive test suites.\n\n**Concurrency Control:** Implements safeguards to prevent workflow conflicts through grouping: *\"cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}\"* ensures the latest version releases on the main branch by canceling older runs.\n\n**File Size Constraints:** Enforces modularity with a hard limit: *\"Enforce a maximum of 1000-1500 lines per code file\"* to keep code within AI context windows and maintain human readability.\n\n**Warnings as Errors:** Static analysis tools treat violations as failures. For example, C# uses *\".NET analyzers (warnings as errors)\"* and Java applies *\"SpotBugs (maximum effort)\"* configurations.\n\n**Deterministic Validation:** The document requires simulating actual merge conditions: *\"CI must test what will actually be merged, not a stale PR snapshot\"* by fetching the base branch and performing a fresh merge before running checks.\n\n**Secrets Detection:** Mandates proactive prevention: *\"Fail CI immediately if secrets are detected\"* and prohibits logging sensitive values.\n\nThe document notably does **not** address flaky tests, test isolation, false positives/negatives, retries, timeouts, caching, or matrix builds."
