[2026-07-22T21:30:37.578Z] [INFO]         "content": "=== serve_and_curl.sh ===\n2:# Boot formal-ai serve, wait for health, run a curl against it, tear down.\n3:# All in one process tree so the environment does not reap the server.\n6:# hand-written /v1/chat/completions payload — useful when isolating server-side\n12:LOG=\"/tmp/formal-ai-serve-$PORT.log\"\n14:FORMAL_AI_AGENT_MODE=1 \"$BIN\" serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port \"$PORT\" > \"$LOG\" 2>&1 &\n20:  \"http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/health\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"server never came up\"; cat \"$LOG\"; exit 1; }\n21:echo \"== server up ==\"\n=== capture_all.sh (does it start serve itself or call others?) ===\n5:# It drives the REAL `@link-assistant/agent` CLI over the OpenAI-compatible server\n6:# for every issue-#538 recipe axis (tomato, potato, diagrams, self-AST), so the\n8:# Each section is the verbatim stdout of `run_agent_cli.sh` for that recipe, which\n13:#   experiments/agent_cli_e2e/capture_all.sh > docs/case-studies/issue-538/agent-cli-e2e-run.log\n17:# lives in the issue_538_agentic tests and reproduce-issue-538.sh.\n24:RUN=\"experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\"\n34:echo \"# Meaning search/fetch turns use the committed MCP fixture for reproducible Wikidata evidence.\"",
