[2026-07-22T21:45:32.196Z] [INFO]         "content": "84\tguide defines the fixture markers, logging proxy assertions, phrasing matrices,\n85\tand CI shape needed to prove that a result came from Formal AI and that the\n86\tclient actually executed the expected tools.\n87\t\n88\t### Replaying the self-coding loop\n89\t\n90\t```bash\n91\tcargo build --release --bin formal-ai\n92\texamples/self-coding/run.sh\n93\tcargo test self_coding_session_replays\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\tFor a real GitHub issue, run `examples/self-coding/run.sh --live ISSUE_URL`.\n97\tThis invokes `solve ISSUE_URL --tool agent --model formal-ai`: Hive Mind drives\n98\tthe Agent CLI, which drives the local Formal AI server.\n99\t\n100\t### Recording self-authorship\n101\t\n102\tThe release metric counts a commit as Formal AI-authored only when its commit\n103\tmessage records both trailers below:\n104\t\n105\t```text\n106\tFormal-AI-Session: <session-id>\n107\tFormal-AI-Evidence: <repo-relative committed evidence path>\n108\t```\n109\t\n110\tThe evidence file must exist in that commit and contain both `formal-ai` and\n111\tthe exact session id. Add one pair per session when multiple sessions authored\n112\ta commit. Do not add these trailers to a human-authored or manually corrected\n113\tcommit; an honest 0% release is valid. The metric counts additions plus\n114\tdeletions from non-merge commits and ignores binary files. Reproduce it with\n115\t`rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --since <previous-tag>`.\n116\t\n117\t## Development Setup\n118\t\n119\t1. **Fork and clone the repository**\n120\t\n121\t   ```bash\n122\t   git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/formal-ai.git\n123\t   cd formal-ai\n124\t   ```\n125\t\n126\t2. **Install Rust**\n127\t\n128\t   Install Rust using rustup (if not already installed):"
