m the original pre-summary session): \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/828 / Your prepared branch: issue-828-4962df13517a / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784753385026 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/829 / Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/828/pulls/829 folder. / Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help. / If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off. / If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code. / Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them. / Proceed.\"\n   - \"Continue from where you left off.\" (continuation nudge)\n   - The system-provided continuation message with the full prior-conversation summary (a harness message, not a new user task).\n   - The final \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY … create a detailed summary\" message (a harness/system summarization instruction, NOT a new task).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Confirm the \"Self-Hosting Evidence Check\" turns GREEN on PR #829 after the push (it was \"in_progress\" at the last poll).\n   - Verify all other CI checks (Detect Changes, Version Modification Check were in_progress; Create Changelog PR skipped; E2E job is expected to SKIP on this PR since gated on .rs changes — decide/document acceptability).\n   - Update `dev/log/issues/828/pulls/829/ANALYSIS.md` to document the self-hosting ratchet resolution (was about to do this).\n   - Confirm R3/R4 (templates comparison + hive-mind best-practices) and R8 (upstream reports) are complete in ANALYSIS.md §7/§8; file upstream issue(s) if the same shared-state pattern exists in the three templates.\n   - Update PR #829 title/description to reflect the ratchet-resolution commits.\n   - Move PR out of draft (`gh pr ready 829`) once all checks are green.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request, I had successfully resolved the failing Self-Hosting Evidence Check. I: (a) drove formal-ai (via the new harness `experiments/issue-828-self-hosting-evidence/run.sh`) to author a genuine `self-source-links.lino` projection (115 counted self-authored lines) with real session `ses_074304d74ffeZbrmkBztcWvOEI`; (b) committed the evidence bundle as `83ab8141` with proper `Formal-AI-Session`/`Formal-AI-Evidence` trailers, and the harness as trailer-free commit `8af51ad4`; (c) verified with the authoritative `rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs` — trailer validation gave \"21.58% (115/533 changed lines; 1/4 commits)\" exit 0, and `--check-ratchet origin/main --until HEAD` gave \"self-hosting ratchet holds against origin/main\" exit 0; (d) pushed (`1e2e1d1c..8af51ad4`). I then polled CI (Self-Hosting Evidence Check \"in_progress\") and ran `grep -n` on ANALYSIS.md to find where to document the ratchet resolution. Branch HEAD is `8af51ad4`; commits ahead of origin/main: `8af51ad4` (harness), `83ab8141` (evidence, trailered), `1e2e1d1c` (E2E memory-isolation fix), `abaeff1a` (initial task details).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Poll CI to confirm the Self-Hosting Evidence Check completed GREEN on the pushed HEAD `8af51ad4` (last status was \"in_progress\"), then update `dev/log/issues/828/pulls/829/ANALYSIS.md` to add a section documenting the ratchet resolution — directly continuing the work I left off (I had just run `grep -n '^#...' dev/log/issues/828/pulls/829/ANALYSIS.md` to locate the insertion point). This directly serves issue #828's mandate to \"fix them all\" and get \"everything totally done.\" After CI confirms green and ANALYSIS.md is updated, verify no other checks regressed, update the PR #829 description, and (if all green) run `gh pr ready 829`. I will NOT fabricate any Formal-AI authorship trailers — per CONTRIBUTING.md, \"an honest 0% release is valid\" and trailers must never be added to hand-authored commits.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1784753385026/d76d13c2-6660-447b-84d5-ad48d489a436.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
