[2026-07-22T21:57:50.729Z] [INFO]         "content": "1\t# Issue #828 — CI/CD false positives/negatives/warnings/errors: analysis\n2\t\n3\t- **Issue:** [link-assistant/formal-ai#828](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/828)\n4\t- **PR:** [#829](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/829)\n5\t- **Branch:** `issue-828-4962df13517a`\n6\t- **Analyst run date:** 2026-07-22\n7\t- **Default branch:** `main` @ `800edd3a` (merge of PR #823 from `issue-822-b85211754f9e`)\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Data collected (this folder)\n10\t\n11\t| File | What it is |\n12\t| --- | --- |\n13\t| `issue-828.json` | Issue #828 body/labels/comments snapshot |\n14\t| `run-29953691265-summary.json` | The failing **CI/CD Pipeline** run job list (main) |\n15\t| `ci-logs/run-29953691265-full.log` | Full run log (26,249 lines) |\n16\t| `ci-logs/run-29953691265-failed.log` | Failed-job-only log (the E2E #687 step) |\n17\t| `ci-logs/687-failure-excerpt.txt` | Clean, de-prefixed excerpt of the failing step |\n18\t| `ci-logs/passing-run-29937886917-e2e687.log` | Prior **passing** main run E2E job (used `run_agent_cli.sh`, pre-687 wiring) |\n19\t| `research/templates-and-best-practices.md` | External template + hive-mind best-practices findings |\n20\t| `repro/` | Local reproduction artifacts (build log + repro runs) |\n21\t\n22\t## 2. Timeline / sequence of events\n23\t\n24\t1. `5e4e5b6a` — issue #687 E2E introduced (`run_issue_687.sh`), 4 CLI turns, assertion `posts >= 9`.\n25\t2. `2765db83` — \"prevent agent cli report compaction\" (context-limit knob raised).\n26\t3. `c5b27a65` — \"remove two nondeterministic CI failures\".\n27\t4. `75341798` — **\"test: confirm reports in research workflow\"**: turns grew 4 → 6 (added `report_destination` + `report_context`), and the assertion was tightened **`posts >= 9` → `posts >= 11`**.\n28\t5. `43208edd` — \"fix(ci): isolate every Agent E2E dependency\".\n29\t6. These landed on `issue-822-b85211754f9e`; PR #823 merged them to `main` as `800edd3a`.\n30\t7. Run **29953691265** (first CI/CD Pipeline on `main` after the merge) **failed** with:\n31\t   `!! expected at least 11 chat rounds, got 10`.\n32\t   All other jobs (lint, test, coverage, local E2E, build, secrets) passed.\n33\t\n34\tThe prior *passing* main run (29937886917, commit `7fa4c25`) predates the 687 wiring in that job's step layout, so it never exercised the `>= 11` assertion — i.e. the assertion had **never run on `main` before it failed**. It was calibrated on the PR branch only.\n35\t\n36\t## 3. Requirements extracted from the issue\n37\t\n38\t| # | Requirement | Status |\n39\t| --- | --- | --- |\n40\t| R1 | Fix the failing default-branch CI/CD run (CI/CD Pipeline 29953691265). | Addressed — see §4/§6 |\n41\t| R2 | Find **all** false positives, false negatives, warnings, and errors in CI/CD and fix them. | Audited — see §5 |\n42\t| R3 | Compare against the three pipeline templates (Rust/JS/Python) and adopt best practices; if the same problem exists in a template, file an issue there. | See `research/` + §7 |\n43\t| R4 | Follow the hive-mind CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md. | See `research/` |\n44\t| R5 | Apply the fix **everywhere** the same problem exists in the codebase (not just one spot). | See §5 audit + §6 |\n45\t| R6 | If data is insufficient for root cause, add debug output / verbose mode (default off). | See §6 (per-turn round diagnostics) |\n46\t| R7 | Do everything in this single PR (#829). | In progress |\n47\t\n48\t## 4. Root cause of the failing test\n49\t\n50\t**Symptom:** `run_issue_687.sh` asserts `posts >= 11` where `posts = grep -c 'POST /v1/chat/completions'` in the server log. On `main` it observed **10**, so the job failed. The count is a proxy for \"the 6-turn research→report→recall→learn agentic workflow made enough tool-call rounds\"."
