[2026-07-22T22:00:38.835Z] [INFO]         "content": "1\t# CI/CD templates & best-practices reference (issue #828)\n2\t\n3\tCollected 2026-07-22 via `gh`/WebFetch from the three pipeline templates and the\n4\thive-mind best-practices doc.\n5\t\n6\t## hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md — key rules\n7\t\n8\t- **Fast-fail ordering:** run fast checks (compile/lint/file-size, ~7–30s) before\n9\t  slow checks (full test suites, ~1–10 min).\n10\t- **Concurrency control:** group runs and cancel superseded ones;\n11\t  `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}` (templates use the\n12\t  inverse — non-main cancels, main runs complete so releases finish).\n13\t- **File size limit:** enforce a maximum of 1000–1500 lines per code file.\n14\t- **Warnings as errors:** static analysis violations fail the build.\n15\t- **Validate the actual merge result (determinism):** \"CI must test what will\n16\t  actually be merged, not a stale PR snapshot\" — fresh-merge the base branch first.\n17\t- **Secrets detection:** fail CI immediately if secrets are detected.\n18\t\n19\t> The doc does **not** explicitly cover flaky-test handling, test isolation,\n20\t> retries, per-job timeouts, caching, or matrix builds — those appear only as\n21\t> concrete implementation choices in the templates.\n22\t\n23\t## Template workflow inventories\n24\t\n25\t- **rust-…-template** `.github/workflows/`: `release.yml` (single combined CI/CD).\n26\t- **js-…-template**: `example-app.yml`, `links.yml`, `release.yml`.\n27\t- **python-…-template**: `docs.yml`, `release.yml`.\n28\t\n29\t## Rust template `release.yml` — observed settings\n30\t\n31\t- Least-privilege `permissions: contents: read`.\n32\t- Global `env: RUSTFLAGS: -Dwarnings`; clippy `--all-targets --all-features`;\n33\t  `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; rustdoc gate `RUSTDOCFLAGS: -D warnings`.\n34\t- **Determinism enforced via a Cargo.lock Guard job** (same dependency graph every\n35\t  run), not via test retries. Tests: `cargo test --all-features --verbose` +\n36\t  `cargo test --doc`. No retries, no nextest, no `--test-threads`.\n37\t- Network flake hardening: `CARGO_NET_RETRY: '10'`, `CARGO_HTTP_MULTIPLEXING: 'false'`.\n38\t- Concurrency: `group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}`,\n39\t  `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}`.\n40\t- Every job sets `timeout-minutes` (5–60).\n41\t- Caching: `actions/cache@v5` on cargo registry/git/target keyed by `Cargo.lock`.\n42\t- Matrix: `test` job over `[ubuntu, macos, windows]` with `fail-fast: false`.\n43\t- `detect-changes` gates downstream jobs by changed file class.\n44\t\n45\t## Relevance to issue #828\n46\t\n47\tThe failing item is a **flaky agent-CLI E2E assertion**, a class the best-practices\n48\tdoc does not explicitly address and the templates do not carry (the templates have\n49\tno shared-state agent-E2E harness). The Rust template's determinism philosophy —\n50\t\"make CI reproducible; test the real merge; pin inputs\" — maps directly onto the\n51\tformal-ai fix: **pin/isolate the E2E server's memory input** so each test is\n52\treproducible, rather than loosen the threshold.\n53\t\n54\tBecause the templates ship no equivalent non-isolated shared-state E2E harness,\n55\tthere is **no matching template defect to report upstream** for this specific bug.\n56\t"
